  "logline": "On Halloween, Michael dresses as Jan to impress the real Jan, who arrives for a surprise visit while Dwight spies and Jim and Pam's prank spirals.",
  "outline": "A: Michael comes as Jan; Jan visits, cuts him down, then gives a small honest moment. B: Dwight, dressed as a nobleman, spies on Jan to learn whom Michael trusts; Jim and Pam's prank on him escalates. C: Ryan in a startup tee, waiting on David. Order: cold, A, B, A, C, B, A, B, A, tag",
  "theme": "Everyone wants to be seen as who they really are, not their costume.",
  "storySoFar": "Michael's dinner with Jan was canceled; the office gave him warm moments. Ryan pitched a website to David Wallace, who said he'd look at it. Dwight campaigns for Assistant Regional Manager, owes beet refunds; Jim holds one real beet. Pam keeps Jim's lamp on; Roy keeps canceling. On Halloween, Michael dressed as Jan; Jan visited unannounced, mocked it, then gave a small kind word. Dwight spied on Jan as Lord Schrute. Jim and Pam's prank on Dwight got out of hand. Ryan wore a startup tee, and Jan noticed his pitch.",
